\section{The one step you must take before prep_surv()}{

The registry codes cause of death with a value -- \code{"Alive or dead of other cause"} -- that is carried by living subjects \strong{and} by those who died of
something else. It cannot be handed to \code{\link[=prep_surv]{prep_surv()}} as
\code{cause_other_value}: the function refuses a declared cause of death on a
living subject, and it is right to, because that same check is what catches
a genuine status/cause contradiction everywhere else.

Resolve the ambiguity first, in data preparation, where \code{vital_status} is
at hand to resolve it with:

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode">}}\preformatted{raw$cause_of_death <- ifelse(
  raw$cause_of_death == "Alive or dead of other cause",
  ifelse(raw$vital_status == "Dead", "Other cause", NA),
  raw$cause_of_death)
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

\code{sim_gist} ships with those two lines already applied -- that is why its
cause column reads \code{"Other cause"} and \code{NA} rather than the registry
