will need them.

The alternative is to leave \code{cause_other_value} at its default \code{NULL} and
let open coding sweep the undeclared label into \code{event_cr = 2}. That gives
the same numbers here and costs the whole closed set: a registry code
nobody anticipated, or a typo, would also become a death from other causes,
silently. Preparing the column instead keeps the closed set intact, and an
unexpected value on a dead subject remains an error.

Whichever route you take, read \code{attr(d, "os_cr_table")} and the counts in
\code{attr(d, "prep_surv")} before going further.
